nd bean-bag areas.","short_summary":"A large newer park oriented around field and court recreation.","evidence_claim":"The Village describes Discovery Park at 300 S. HighPoint Drive as a 51-acre site with soccer fields, basketball courts, sand volleyball courts, and bean-bag areas.","source_url":"https://www.romeoville.org/CivicAlerts.aspx?AID=1508&ARC=2246","source_title":"Romeoville Enhances Parks and Open Space","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":"2019-07-19","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"This is an outdoor park; plan for daylight and weather conditions.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"romeo-crossing-park","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Romeo Crossing Park","title":"Romeo Crossing Park","subtitle":"West Romeo Road corridor","notes":"Explore the accessible playground and challenge course, or use the perimeter-area trails and open athletic space for a daytime outing.","short_summary":"A new inclusive community park centered on adaptive and accessible play.","evidence_claim":"The Village lists Romeo Crossing Park at 400 W. Romeo Road with Illinois’ only lighted adaptive sports field, an ADA playground, a sled hill, dog parks, and fitness course.","source_url":"https://romeoville.org/facilities/facility/details/Romeo-Crossing-Park-171","source_title":"Romeo Crossing Park","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The Village notes a 0.64-mile perimeter walking path as coming soon; use currently available features only.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"village-park","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Village Park","title":"Village Park","subtitle":"West Romeo Road corridor","notes":"Head here for court or field recreation; the Village’s facility inventory lists tennis courts, five basebal